## Problem Analysis

The build fails because `realpath` is not declared. Under `-std=c11`, even with `_POSIX_C_SOURCE=200809L`, the compiler doesn't see the declaration (the error is consistent across all three call sites). The checkpoint tests then fail because the binary was never produced.

## Fix

Replace all `realpath`-based self-copy detection with an inode-comparison helper (`stat` is always available via `<sys/stat.h>` which is already included). This eliminates the dependency on `realpath` entirely.

### Changes to `src/c_cp/c_cp.c`

**1. Add a new static helper function immediately after the closing brace of `copy_path` (before `copy_recursive`):**

```c
static int same_or_descendant(const char *ref, const char *path) {
    struct stat st_ref, st_cur;
    if (stat(ref, &st_ref) != 0) return 0;

    size_t len = strlen(path);
    if (len == 0 || len >= 4096) return 0;

    char buf[4096];
    memcpy(buf, path, len + 1);

    for (;;) {
        if (stat(buf, &st_cur) == 0 &&
            st_cur.st_dev == st_ref.st_dev && st_cur.st_ino == st_ref.st_ino)
            return 1;
        char *slash = strrchr(buf, '/');
        if (!slash) return 0;
        *slash = '\0';
        if (buf[0] == '\0') {
            if (stat("/", &st_cur) == 0 &&
                st_cur.st_dev == st_ref.st_dev && st_cur.st_ino == st_ref.st_ino)
                return 1;
            return 0;
        }
    }
}
```

**2. In `copy_recursive`, replace the entire directory self-copy detection block.** Delete from the line `char src_real[4096];` through the end of the `else` branch that contains `mkdir(dst, ...)` (i.e., the whole block that starts with `char src_real[4096];` and ends just before the `/* Recurse into directory entries */` comment). Replace it with:

