### Summary of what changed

| What | Why |
|------|-----|
| Added `same_or_descendant` helper | Detects self-copy / ancestor-descendant via `stat` inode comparison; no `realpath` needed |
| Removed all three `realpath` calls and the string-comparison logic | Eliminates the implicit-declaration error under `-std=c11` |
| Self-copy check now: `same_or_descendant(src, dst)` (dst exists) or `same_or_descendant(src, parent_of_dst)` (dst missing) | Semantically equivalent to the old realpath-prefix comparison, plus handles alias (same inode, different path) cases |

